## Why This Is Asked

Tests advanced Terraform design across multi-cloud per-tenant isolation, secret management, and policy enforcement. It also probes testing discipline and scalable module composition.

## Key Concepts

- Terraform provider aliases per tenant
- Tenant-scoped remote backends with encryption
- Vault-backed credentials retrieval
- Per-tenant RBAC and network segmentation
- Idempotence testing with Terratest
- Policy gates with OPA or Sentinel

## Code Example

```hcl
variable "tenants" {
  type = map(object({ cloud = string, region = string }))
}

provider "aws" {
  alias  = "tenant_${each.key}"
  region = var.tenants[each.key].region
  # fetch creds from Vault here
}

provider "azurerm" {
  alias   = "tenant_${each.key}"
  features = {}
}

terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    key = "state/${each.key}/terraform.tfstate"
    encryption = true
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evolve the design to support adding a new cloud to the tenant mix?
- How would you structure tests to run in parallel for many tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-repo data sharing and multi-region provider patterns, plus a practical gating approach to prevent drift.

## Key Concepts
- Provider aliasing across regions
- data.terraform_remote_state for read-only cross-repo data
- Per-region backends and workflows
- CI policy gates to enforce drift checks and approvals
- Cross-region resource referencing of VPC/subnet IDs

## Code Example
```javascript
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.3"
}
provider "aws" {
  alias  = "east"
  region = "us-east-1"
}
provider "aws" {
  alias  = "west"
  region = "us-west-2"
}
data "terraform_remote_state" "net" {
  backend = "s3"
  config = {
    bucket = "infra-network-bucket"
    key    = "network/us-east-1/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
# usage
resource "aws_instance" "web" {
  provider    = aws.west
  ami         = "ami-0abcdef1234567890"
  subnet_id   = data.terraform_remote_state.net.outputs.public_subnet_id
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift detection across repos? 
- How would you handle regional failover and state restoration?
